Negative control for the refused record being ONE unit (`F4` · `G7` · `AC6.4`).

Moves the invalid ring off the record's row GROUP and back onto the row itself,
which is the R6 re-drive-1 defect verbatim: the ring closes at the bottom of the
49px row and the reason strip sits in a box below it, outside the mark. The
mutation is the plausible wrong implementation rather than a disabled variant —
the row IS the element that failed, so ringing it looks right and is wrong.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: `list-surface-row-ring.spec.ts` — the ring host no longer holds the row's
`[role="alert"]`, so "encloses the refused row and the reason together" and
"leaves the next record plainly outside it" both fail, and the three
one-vocabulary cases fail with it because the host that carries the ring is no
longer the `<tbody>` the group marks invalid.

